<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Laconia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lakonia, Lacedaemon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Laconia is a region of the south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, centred on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eurotas">Eurotas</a> valley between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taygetus">Taygetus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parnon">Parnon</a> mountains. In the Mycenaean age it held the kingdom remembered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homer">Homer</a> as that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelaus">Menelaus</a>, and from the Archaic period it was the territory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>. It is now a regional unit with its capital at Sparta.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/laconia.jpg" alt="Laconia" width="320" height="370" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Badseed; derivative work by Pitichinaccio · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2010_Dimi_Lakonias_numbered.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Epaminondas then invaded <b>Laconia</b>, built a fleet in 364 BCE and died winning the Battle of Mantinea in 362 BCE.</blockquote><a href="/empire/boeotian-league">Boeotian League · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Sparta lay in the valley of the Eurotas River in <b>Laconia</b>, in the south-eastern Peloponnese, between the Taygetus and Parnon mountain ranges.</blockquote><a href="/empire/sparta">Sparta · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>At the bottom the helots, bound to the land of <b>Laconia</b> and Messenia, outnumbered the citizens many times over.</blockquote><a href="/societies/sparta">Social Hierarchy of Ancient Sparta</a></li><li><blockquote>It joined Thebes in invading <b>Laconia</b> and supported the refounding of Messene.</blockquote><a href="/state/arcadian-league">Arcadian League</a></li><li><blockquote>Its purpose was to control the independent-minded population of the Mani and the route into <b>Laconia</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/barony-of-passavant">Barony of Passavant</a></li><li><blockquote>The Ezeritai, whose name probably comes from the Slavic word for lake, settled in the marshy plain of Helos in southern <b>Laconia</b> during the Slavic migrations into the Peloponnese of the late 6th and 7th centuries.</blockquote><a href="/state/ezeritai">Ezeritai</a></li></ul></section>
